{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791642239,"nonce":"/EFJvKTcPnjk8CdcYG+pWk2NNj0=","message":"First slice is committed on branch hot-reload-structural, which is not on main yet:\n\n- e3208ed5ed9f627c6289c3988fa5eb34fe68fdfa ash: leave pool indices out of the hash a reload compares\n- 25e360afba853614e6885441838533d2c9ae8081 ash: hash a dynamic field access by the name it reads\n- 067880a4249fb4acc775829ca14c3911620ea99c ash: reload a program that adds, removes or moves closures\n- d6c4b79c16dfafd51b5d99e4699d63de1a44bdf5 ash: test a reload that adds, removes, moves and edits closures\n- 69c99cdf281e44686bfc05ab6ff03f5099ab8219 docs: say what a hot reload can change\n\nWhat it does: a reload takes closures added, removed, moved and edited, and natives the new code is the first to use. ashui's tests/fixtures/hotreload v3 reloads with the panel's state kept (count=5, width 100, height 10) under the default ladder, --jit-threshold 1, --jit-tier cranelift and --jit-tier llvm; v2 and v4 are unchanged. On ashui's program the read takes about 4 ms and the renumbering about 11 ms.\n\nChecks: ash_core 113, ash_interp 7 and air 205 unit tests; tests/hot_reload_closures (four edits, each under four tier arrangements) and osr_retier, ref_args, f32_tier_parity, retyped_reads, fma_promotion_parity, wide_hybrid, llvm_worker_pool, parity_matrix and stdlib_matrix on the Mac; unit conformance on hybrid 1069/1069; scripts/test_hot_reload.sh with and without --jit-threshold 1. On the NUC (x86_64): ash_core lib tests and hot_reload_closures.\n\nStill refused, with a message: a method added or removed (the class's vtable would move), a new type ahead of the last object type, a new class or static (the globals array is fixed), and a program that needs more function slots than were reserved (8192, or as many again as the program started with).\n\nDifferences to know about:\n- An edit and an addition in one list of closures: the edited closure is taken as a new one, so a closure made before the reload keeps its old body until it is replaced. Closures edited alone, in place, are taken as edits.\n- A dropped function stays in the table for good; one that comes back with the same body takes its slot again.\n- --mode jit flags a reload and never applies it. This is so on main as well.\n\nLeft for the next slice: methods (vtable growth), types (the C type table and the copies the tiers hold), classes and statics (the globals array).","files":null}]}